From 4ea95a688d5b5ce086f198ce0d8b3967b2d1aa5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: horizon-prism <horizon-prism@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:32:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Horizon mods page (M5)

- HorizonMod scans horizon-mods/ (.hmod, folder mods) and
  horizon-native-mods/ (.hnmod, .hmod) and reads both manifests from the
  zip or the folder;
- HorizonModList parses and writes horizon-mods.txt with the game's rules:
  content mods off until mod.<id>:true, native mods on until
  mod.<id>:false, key.* lines preserved;
- HorizonModsPage lists the mods with a checkbox, status column and
  Add/Remove/Refresh/Open folder actions; broken files stay visible and
  removable;
- Horizon instances no longer show the Java mod pages;
- HorizonMod_test covers parsing, serialization, scanning and disk round
  trips (9 tests).

Native mods are listed but not built into the game: this fork runs a
prebuilt horizon-client, so the page says so instead of pretending.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
